On Mon, Apr 19, 2010 at 6:37 PM, tijlan <jbotijlan@gmail.com> wrote:
>
>  Also, according to jbofi'e, "cei"
> would assign "carna'ivinji" only to the tertau "vinji":
>
> =A0[ ( ti ) << | | carna nalci | vinji cei carna'ivinji | >> ]
>
> (... which appears to me odd though, since the official definition says t=
he
> target of "cei" is a selbri, not a brivla, and this "vinji" is not an
> individual selbri.)

It's actually something in between: a tanru unit. Syntactically you can do:

    ke carna nalci vinji ke'e cei carna'ivinji

which identifies the tanru unit "ke carna nalci vinji ke'e" with the
tanru unit "carna'ivinji".

> I should have used "zei":
>
> =A0ti carna zei nalci zei vinji cei carna'ivinji
> =A0[ ( ti ) << | carna zei nalci zei vinji | cei carna'ivinji >> ]

Yes, that works, "carna zei nalci zei vinji" and "carna'ivinji" are
the same lujvo.

